Q: localStorage data is removed when opening a Bootstrap modal A: <p>You are partway there... you already discovered that the selectpicker returns an empty array for the modal, the handler can't tell the difference between that and a real user selection so it overwrites with the empty value.</p>
<p>You probably don't want the &quot;don't save if empty&quot; workaround, because what if a user genuinely deselects everything? The more robust fix is to ignore programmatic changes. A change fired by real user interaction has <code>event.originalEvent</code> set to the native browser event, while a change fired by a library call internally does not.</p>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>$(document).on(&quot;change&quot;, &quot;#division_selectpicker_form #division_selectpicker&quot;, function(event) {
  if (!event.originalEvent) return; // ignore programmatic changes (e.g. selectpicker refresh)
  var value = $(this).val();
  localStorage.setItem('user_divisions', value);
});
</code></pre>
<p>If your version of the bootstrap library acutally does dispatch a real event object, this check won't catch it. In that case, set a flag (like <code>isRefreshing = true</code>) before code that calls the selectpicker, check for it in your event handler, and clear the flag after.</p>

Q: How to parameterize agent pool name in azure pipeline with yaml file A: <p>This issue can be solved by using the answer in this issue: <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/58698996/azure-devops-is-it-possible-to-nest-yaml-templates-inside-another-yaml-template">Azure Devops: Is it possible to nest yaml templates inside another yaml template?</a>.</p>
<p><strong>Copyed from link:</strong>
refer code:</p>
<pre><code>parameters:
  buildArtifactName: &quot;build&quot;
  solution: &quot;&quot;

jobs:
- job: 'BuildSolution'
  pool:
    vmImage: ${{parameters.vmImage}}
    continueOnError: false
  variables:
    artifactName: ${{ parameters.buildArtifactName}}
  steps:
    - task: NuGetCommand@2
      displayName: 'Restore NuGet packages'
      inputs:
        restoreSolution: ${{ parameters.solutionDir }}/${{ parameters.solution }}
        configuration: ${{parameters.buildConfiguration}}
</code></pre>
